from pathlib import Path
p=Path('build_manuscript.py');s=p.read_text()
s=s.replace('Thirty-eight','Forty-four')
a=s.index('"Abstract—');b=s.index('\n"",',a)
s=s[:a]+'''"Abstract—Tool-using agents can leave duplicated, unauthorized or unresolved service effects despite plausible final answers. FA-MAS specifies contract-constrained recovery under latency, cost and state-risk limits. Its reference implementation enforces reduced gates and ranks finite recovery actions; full subgraph recomposition, calibrated diagnosis and multi-agent coordination remain proposed extensions. An original 52,500-row authored simulator uses unequal diagnosis parameters and a weaker terminal criterion, preventing causal interpretation of favorable safety contrasts. An initial 18,000-row matched exploratory study fails to demonstrate safety superiority. A further 18,000-row defect-correction study restricts compensation to existing uncertain effects, aligns selection and budgets, and counts detected unauthorized execution as unsafe. Corrected FA-MAS records 7.58% unsafe outcomes versus 9.67% without gates and 8.93% with first-feasible selection, but its difference from no-compensation is unresolved. These post-audit contrasts remain conditional on authored probabilities. Two local HTTP/SQLite implementations expose compatibility and cleanup behavior. An additional 150 direct-tool checks use 25 cancellation tasks from pinned public retail and airline code. After lost cancellation replies, reconciliation avoids repeated airline refund history; retail rejects repetition itself. These are reference-action mechanism checks, not conversational benchmark scores. A hash-locked clean dependency installation reproduces all simulator rows and public-tool traces. A bounded live-model protocol is implemented but unexecuted. The contribution is a recovery specification, executable mechanism evaluation and transparent limitations; no live-model or production advantage is claimed.",''' +s[b:]
s=s.replace('With matched diagnosis and a stricter orphan-state criterion, FA-MAS does not improve safety over the tested simpler controls.', 'The initial matched study is negative. After disclosed defect corrections, the exploratory simulator favors gated selection over two controls but shows no resolved benefit from compensation; orphan-state failures persist.')
s=s.replace('the matched negative result prevents a claim of demonstrated safety superiority.', 'the matched and corrected sensitivity studies prevent an unconditional claim of safety superiority.')
s=s.replace('The matched exploratory study does not demonstrate safety superiority.', 'The initial matched exploratory study is negative; the corrected study remains conditional and does not establish production or live-model superiority.')
s=s.replace('an untested container recipe and a read-only replay auditor. Tests and replay pass in the current environment. An independent clean installation, transitive environment lock, archival DOI, rights-cleared license and author-confirmed citation metadata remain incomplete.', 'a digest-pinned unbuilt container recipe, a read-only replay auditor and a transitive wheel-hash lock for CPython 3.12 Linux x86_64. A fresh virtual environment reproduces all observations on this host. Independent replication, a container build, archival DOI, rights-cleared license and author-confirmed citation metadata remain incomplete.')
s=s.replace('a direct-dependency pin file,', 'a complete scoped dependency pin file,')
# Remove one duplicated paragraph describing the same historical paired contrasts.
start=s.index('"Under the original unequal authored diagnosis parameters');end=s.index('\n',start);s=s[:start]+s[end+1:]
# Insert additions before existing manuscript assembly.
